### Competitor Analysis & Fact-Check Summary

* **Supplied Competitor URL:** `https://www.caratlane.com/blog/kids-earrings-collection/`
* **Competitor Strengths:** Highlighted Indian cultural piercing significance (Namakaran/Mundan), discussed basic hoop vs stud trade-offs, and mentioned nickel-free metals.
* **Competitor Weaknesses Addressed by BlueStone:** 
  * Competitor lacked specific focus on infant/baby starter earrings (Karnavedha, Annaprashan, 0-12 months).
  * Lacked technical detail on safety clasps (covered dome screw backs vs open butterfly push backs).
  * Missed clear gram weight guidelines (0.8g to 1.5g per pair limit) and BIS 6-digit HUID hallmarking standards.
* **Authoritative Standards Integrated:**
  * Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) mandatory HUID hallmarking for 18kt (750), 14kt (585), and 22kt (916).
  * Paediatric piercing guidelines on sterile saline aftercare, avoiding harsh alcohols, and 6-8 week starter stud healing intervals.

